    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130-a3">

                <pb facs="0249" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg153"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Translation of an imperial decree published in the
                        Manuscript Pekin Gazette, June 14, 1900.</hi></head>
                <p>Chung Li and others have memorialized us detailing circumstances of the burning
                    of the Christian chapels in the districts under the senior and junior police
                    provost of Pekin, and request that punishment may be inflicted upon them.</p>
                <pb facs="0250" n="154" xml:id="pg154"/>
                <p>Let Chung Li, Ying Nien, and Tsai Lan be handed over to the board for the
                    determination of a strict form of penalty. Let the deputy provosts and other
                    officers of the two divisions of the gendarmerie be deprived of their rank, but
                    allowed to remain in office. Let their buttons be taken away, and they are
                    hereby commanded to rigorously arrest the important ringleaders of the outlaws.
                    They must be arrested without fail, and strenuously punished.</p>
            </div>
